    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 83.29. He faces a highly favorable matchup against a pitcher with a 5.68 xERA, and his elite plate discipline paired with a significant platoon advantage makes him the premier start of the slate. Following closely are **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.07); despite facing stiffer competition than **Gunnar Henderson**, both hitters possess the raw talent to exploit their respective matchups, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** specifically benefiting from a positive park factor and a favorable xERA opponent. **Jackson Merrill** also provides elite value at 71.40, boosted significantly by a +14% park advantage that makes him a must-start despite the solid 3.87 xERA of the opposing hurler.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the final utility and bench spots. **Tommy White** (48.09) was the closest to cracking the starting lineup, ultimately edged out by **Drake Baldwin** and **Josh Jung** due to the latter players' superior volume and consistency in their respective slots. **Miguel Vargas** (47.27) also remained on the bench; while his xwOBA remains strong, the combination of a tougher opposing starter (3.54 xERA) and the current team depth pushed him out of the primary nine. We are actively monitoring the status of **Andy Pages**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active depth to maintain offensive output in the SB-starved 5x5 landscape. \n\nRisk management remains a priority today, particularly regarding **Nasim Nunez** (41.02), who faces a difficult challenge against a top-tier pitcher (3.24 xERA). His score hovers just above our 40-point bench floor, and while his elite sprint speed makes him an attractive consideration for our SB requirements, the matchup risk is palpable. Similarly, **Henry Bolte** must navigate a -6% park penalty today; while his leadoff spot adds value, he represents a high-variance play. We are comfortable with these assignments for now, provided that **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** maintains his current efficiency and **Coby Mayo** can capitalize on the platoon advantage provided by the weak opposing pitching staff.",
